# Repo conventions

## Simplicity

Keep repos **simple and easy to navigate**. Minimize file bloat. Do not add audits, traceability scaffolding, or extra layers unless the user asks.

Prefer **compact scripts**: if something fits in ~500 lines, do not inflate it to 1500 for readability. Minimize explanatory comments and excessive blank lines in scripts.

## Secrets and config

Use a **`.env`** file (gitignored) for API keys and tunable parameters (e.g. model names). Do not commit secrets.

## LLMs

Default to **OpenAI** models unless the user chooses otherwise. Prefer current OpenAI APIs / model classes when wiring LLM clients.

## Standard layout (this user)

- **`environment.yml`** — conda env (env name in `name:` field)
- **`requirements.txt`** — pip deps (often referenced from `environment.yml`)
- **`scripts/`** — all project Python; entry points as **`python -m scripts.<name>`**
- **Mac** — paths and shell examples assume macOS
